DTSTART:20260724T080000Z
DTEND:20260724T120000Z
SUMMARY:Never Summer Trail Run
DESCRIPTION:The Never Summer 100km & 60km races take place almost entirely within State Forest State Park\, running between the Never Summer Mountains on the northern border of Rocky Mountain National Park and the Medicine Bow Mountains near Cameron Pass. The 100km course covers 65.7 miles with 14\,500ft of vertical gain at an average elevation of 10\,220ft. The 60km covers 39.2 miles with 8\,100ft of gain. Terrain includes cross country\, jeep and logging roads\, alpine trail\, meadows\, streams\, boulder fields\, and high alpine ridge running reaching up to 11\,852ft. Registration caps at 625 total (325 for 100km\, 300 for 60km). Time limits are 24 hours for 100km and 15 hours for 60km. 100km finishers under 23 hours qualify for the Western States 100 Lottery.
LOCATION:Gould Community Center\, Gould\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
